<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Maymun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Maymun was the leading figure of a family of admirals who had commanded the Almoravid fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>, the chief port and naval base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. When Almería rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in 1145 he became one of its local rulers, during a brief independence ended when Castilian, Aragonese and Genoese forces captured the city in 1147.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-maymun.jpg" alt="Ibn Maymun" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blaisio Ugolino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Moses_Maimonides_in_Thesaurus_antiquitatum_sacrarum.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
